=== 3. OBS-2: NEGATIVE CONTROL on the freshness binding — src/** is NOT in scope ===
Injected in the copy: appended one line to src/cocos/scene-graph/node.ts (engine source, no rebuild):
    frozen sourceHash             = ac1b151596b36975
    after src/** edit (no build)  = ac1b151596b36975   <-- UNCHANGED
    after restore                 = ac1b151596b36975   (node.ts hash bdb87e07142a4d1e == snapshot)
Meaning: recipe/dual-track evidence freshness is bound to the BUILT BUNDLE BYTES, not to engine sources.
An engine-source change that is never rebuilt (or a build/ dir older than src/) leaves every sourceHash
consumer reporting "evidence current". This is the mirror image of F-38/F-39 (existence/bytes bound,
content not): here the binding is real but its INPUT SET is narrower than the thing it certifies.
Not detected by any gate today. Restored; copy re-verified against the manifest afterwards.
Minimal suggestion (needs approval; tools/ only): either add the built-bundle↔src consistency check that
`npm run build` was re-executed (hash src/** into a separate buildStamp and assert buildStamp freshness),
or widen sourceHash's input set to src/** + tools/**. Retest: an src edit without rebuild must flip
v06-report RED; a clean rebuild must return it GREEN.

=== 4. OBS-3: the recipe runner cannot execute outside a git checkout ======
tools/verify/benchmark-evidence.cjs:24 metadata() execFileSync('git','rev-parse HEAD') with no try/catch:
in a .git-less copy it throws status 128 "fatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories)"
and run-recipes-browser.cjs:49 aborts BEFORE running a single recipe (recipes-run.log, nothing executed).
Workaround applied: `git init` + one empty commit inside the copy
(bb80eab), which leaves sourceHash unaffected (ac1b… verified again after init).
Honest classification: fails LOUD, not silent -> harness/robustness defect, non-blocking for release, but it
means the recipe gate is not reproducible in a clean-room or from an npm-installed source tarball
(no .git). Suggested minimal fix: fall back to baseRevision 'unknown' when git is absent.

