=== 6. OBS-4: 'revision' in recipe evidence is decorative (verified by construction) ==
tools/benchmark/recipes/run-recipes-browser.cjs:82,86 store baseRevision/revision from `git rev-parse HEAD`;
`baseRevision` appears in NO validator: grep over tools/benchmark/recipes/schema.ts, run-recipes-browser.cjs,
v06-report.cjs shows zero assertions. My copy produced valid, accepted 30/30 evidence whose revision
(bb80eab…) does not exist in the real repository. Severity is low because sourceHash (content-derived) IS
asserted and cannot be forged without the same inputs — but any doc or human reading `revision` as
provenance is being shown an unchecked field. Minimal suggestion (needs approval): have the gate assert
revision === git rev-parse HEAD of the tree it runs in, or drop the field name to avoid implying binding.

